{"id":"NCT05685745","title":"Multisite Inventory of Neonatal-Perinatal Interventions (MINI) Minimum Dataset","official":"Multisite Inventory of Neonatal-Perinatal Interventions (MINI) Minimum Dataset","summary":"The goal of the Tiny Baby Collaborative Multicenter Inventory of Neonatal-Perinatal Interventions (MINI) minimum dataset is to serve as a registry detailing the outcomes and practices for all deliveries and infants admitted to intensive care at 22-23 weeks' gestation at participating hospitals.","conditions":["Infant, Extremely Premature","Obstetric Labor, Premature","Premature Birth","Intensive Care, Neonatal","Intensive Care Units, Neonatal"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* All local births with gestational ages of 22 weeks 0 days - 23 weeks 6 days, regardless of pregnancy outcome or neonatal intensive care (NICU) admission; AND\n* All outborn NICU admissions with gestational age at birth of 22 weeks 0 days - 23 weeks 6 days\n* Optional: Centers who desire to include data for NICU admissions of infants born \\<22 weeks' gestation may also submit these data.","minAge":"0 Years","maxAge":"1 Year","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":5000,"start":"2019-01-01","pcd":"2030-01-01","upd":"2026-07-06","sponsor":"The University of Texas Health Science Center, Houston","areas":["other"],"central":["Matthew A Rysavy, MD, PhD · 713-500-5651 · Matthew.A.Rysavy@uth.tmc.edu"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35249","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Colm Travers, MD · 205-934-4680 · cptravers@uabmc.edu"},{"f":"University of South Alabama","city":"Mobile","pr":"Alabama","zip":"36688","s":"R","lat":30.6944,"lon":-88.043,"c":"Kalsang Dolma, MD · kdolma@health.southalabama.edu"},{"f":"Vallywise Health Medical Center","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85008","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"Jason Couch, MD · jason_couch@dmgaz.o